e] [17592186426488 1074 "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${x}_{1}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, the initial and terminal points are the same (since the path is closed and is traversed only once). Therefore, ${x}_{1}={x}_{2},$ and we have\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$" 13194139534582 17592186045417 true] [17592186426489 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426487 13194139534582 17592186045417 true] [17592186426489 1069 "q-124308" 13194139534582 17592186045417 true] [17592186426489 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534582 17592186045417 true] [17592186426489 1071 "![](images/fb/fb482ddbb5bde83cfd6ed383b0f321cb27377f34aafcb9e74e44d91824dcf366.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x,$ where $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is the path comprising of a line segment and a semicircle of radius $1,$ as shown above." 13194139534582 17592186045417 true] [17592186426489 1072 #uuid "b6d2ac1d-75ed-5453-8dc7-92123acc1f15" 13194139534582 17592186045417 true] [17592186426489 1074 "The line integral of unity with respect to $x$ along a path $C$ is equal to the net change in $x$ between the terminal and initial points:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the terminal point, and ${x}_{1}$ is the $x$-coordinate of the initial point.\n\nIn our case, ${x}_{2}=-3$ and ${x}_{1}=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}x={x}_{2}-{x}_{1}=(-3)-2=-5.\n$$" 13194139534582 17592186045417 true] [17592186426490 1058 #edb/ref 17592186426493 13194139534582 17592186045417 true] [17592186426490 1062 #uuid "057ed5af-875f-53e1-addf-521f93615e7d" 13194139534582 17592186045417 true] [17592186426490 1063 #edb/ref 17592186259608 13194139534582 17592186045417 true] [17592186426491 1062 #uuid "494b3b4e-68